; newworlddialog.eval - the New world dialog (editor-updates P4), driven by the
; same calls its buttons make (`worlds newdialog ...`).
;
; In a level: pick "Copy one level" with crypt2, create nwd_level, then try the
; same name again (refused, in its own words). On the world screen, with the
; Worlds dialog open BELOW it: create nwd_blank (a fresh Open is blank again),
; and the Worlds dialog must list it and ARM it - one click from going there.
; tools/EditorTest.py phase 10 judges it and removes both worlds.

logecho on
reset
worlds newdialog
worlds newdialog source level crypt2
worlds newdialog create nwd_level
worlds newdialog create nwd_level
worlds newdialog off
echo --- over the worlds dialog ---
worldmap on
worlds dialog
worlds newdialog create nwd_blank
worlds newdialog off
worlds dialog
worldmap off
